{"id": "EUVD-2026-45802", "enisaUuid": "598065dc-c73b-3508-969c-34f8b6636125", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: capture fast-RX rate before mesh reuses skb->cb\n\nieee80211_invoke_fast_rx() reads RX status through\nIEEE80211_SKB_RXCB(skb), which aliases the same skb->cb storage\nthat ieee80211_rx_mesh_data() reuses as IEEE80211_TX_INFO.  In the\nunicast forward path, mesh_data does:\n\n\tinfo = IEEE80211_SKB_CB(fwd_skb);\n\tmemset(info, 0, sizeof(*info));\n\non the same skb the caller still names via rx->skb, then either\nqueues the skb for TX (success) or kfree_skb()'s it (no-route)\nbefore returning RX_QUEUED.  The caller's RX_QUEUED arm then\ncalls sta_stats_encode_rate(status) on memory that is either\nzeroed (success path) or freed (no-route path).  The latter is\nKASAN slab-use-after-free in ieee80211_prepare_and_rx_handle.\n\nFix by encoding the rate from status before invoking\nieee80211_rx_mesh_data(), so the RX_QUEUED arm consumes a value\ncaptured while status was still backed by valid memory.", "datePublished": "2026-07-19T15:40:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:04", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5fe97797412aa8bc0184f78379fafb594bcb7f66", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0cd37e746e98ab0baa6d8b812955220775b080d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2650f8461cd8ba287fee2992b36abe733c2bd5e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2fb64f94f9afb774f2fa0c7835727d7a67f89f07", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d71c841be5d9e586ee7f36c0dc8ed4db0d9a1349"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64117", "GHSA-8c2f-6crq-prr9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "003be28b-5c41-32b6-b8c0-3e0697bcb5d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.11"}, {"id": "1cf5db9e-1277-3b42-a641-e210b917097f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3468e1e0c639032a603450f0830ccabfa76f5806 <5fe97797412aa8bc0184f78379fafb594bcb7f66"}, {"id": "3767ff98-916a-30d8-840f-4362528ef5c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "42dc7b00-db8a-353b-871a-416349f161bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3468e1e0c639032a603450f0830ccabfa76f5806 <0cd37e746e98ab0baa6d8b812955220775b080d6"}, {"id": "4c44596d-738a-339f-a510-14ad0d38cc40", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3468e1e0c639032a603450f0830ccabfa76f5806 <2fb64f94f9afb774f2fa0c7835727d7a67f89f07"}, {"id": "5932b2cb-81ad-3b20-ac19-cfd359668ea2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "5c713515-ac09-3cb7-a1fa-e8637450b30a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3468e1e0c639032a603450f0830ccabfa76f5806 <d71c841be5d9e586ee7f36c0dc8ed4db0d9a1349"}, {"id": "a661d71b-8c5b-314e-943a-f8c6694a09f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "c768110c-7d6e-3176-8fc3-02c47cb13290", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "de65bd8e-9851-3efb-919e-5d660910a680", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4"}, {"id": "e07582fa-2b86-390a-975b-7b22d72672a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3468e1e0c639032a603450f0830ccabfa76f5806 <a2650f8461cd8ba287fee2992b36abe733c2bd5e"}, {"id": "fcf8f234-6b4d-35ed-8109-a63d586f8918", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "30405c51-539f-3d25-899e-98b424a66420", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}